US-009 is complete. Summary of what was done:

**Routes migrated to policies** (`global::is-authenticated` + `global::has-permission` with the code each handler previously enforced):
- `notification`: core find/findOne → session only (controller keeps the recipient filter); create/update/delete → `MANAGE_NOTIFICATIONS`; custom `/notifications/me*` and `/:id/read` → `auth: false` + session.
- `audit`: `/audit-logs`, `/audit-logs/export`, core find/findOne → `VIEW_AUDIT_LOGS`. The custom audit routes keep users-permissions auth (they never had `auth: false`; the seed grants `api::audit.audit.find/export`). Core create/update/delete → session only, since no permission code exists for them and the u-p role gate remains.
- `rol`: writes + `POST/DELETE /rols/:id/permissions` → `MANAGE_ROLES`; reads → session.
- `permission` → `MANAGE_PERMISSIONS`; `setting` → `MANAGE_SETTINGS`.
- users-permissions extension: `/auth/me/permissions` → session; `GET /admin/users` → `VIEW_USERS`; `POST/PUT/DELETE /admin/users` → `MANAGE_USERS`; `/users/:id/anonymize` → `ANONYMIZE_USER`.

**`protectedController.js` removed.** Controllers read `ctx.state.user`; empty overrides were dropped (`setting` is now a bare `createCoreController`). `has-permission.js` now also exports `userHasPermission(user, code)` (attached to the policy function — the Strapi loader registers it unchanged), and `canModifyComment` uses it against `ctx.state.user` instead of `authorize()`.

**Verification:**
- `grep -rn protectedController backend/src` → empty; every `auth: false` route has `policies` in the same config.
- `backend/package.json` untouched; backend has no lint/typecheck rules configured.
- `npm test` (Node 20): **80/80** — 52 existing + 3 unit cases for `userHasPermission` + new `config/env/test/admin/index.js` with 24 HTTP cases covering each migrated route (no token / no permission / with permission, including audit `userId` from `ctx.state.user`).

`progress.md` updated: the "record-dependent permission" pattern now points to `userHasPermission`, plus two new patterns (policies on plugin routes; the `auth: false` grep rule) and the US-009 entry.

